diff --git a/eduka/README.Eduka.md b/eduka/README.Eduka.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..768d363
--- /dev/null
+++ b/eduka/README.Eduka.md
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+# Eduka-Orca
+
+Eduka-Orca adalah pembaca layar **Orca 50.3** yang disesuaikan untuk
+**Edukasaun OS** dan desktop **Eduka-Desktop (LXQt)**, dengan fokus pada
+pengguna dengan **gangguan pendengaran (tunarungu ringan–sedang)** dan
+tunanetra.
+
+*Eduka-Orca is the Orca 50.3 screen reader tuned for Edukasaun OS and the
+Eduka-Desktop (LXQt), with a focus on users who are hard of hearing. An English
+summary is at the end.*
+
+## Apa yang berbeda dari Orca biasa
+
+| | Orca (upstream) | Eduka-Orca |
+|---|---|---|
+| Kecepatan bicara | 50 (dari 0–100) | **30** — lebih pelan, tidak terburu-buru |
+| Nada suara | 5.0 | **4.5** — sedikit lebih rendah, lebih mudah didengar |
+| Volume | 10 (maksimum) | 10 (maksimum) |
+| Teks ucapan di layar (*speech monitor*) | mati | **nyala**, huruf 24 pt, kuning di atas hitam, menempel di bawah layar seperti subtitle, tidak merebut fokus keyboard, kalimat terbaru ditebalkan |
+| Bahasa Tetum | jatuh ke suara Inggris | **memakai suara Portugis (Eropa)** karena eSpeak NG belum punya suara Tetum |
+| Desktop LXQt | tidak ada autostart | autostart LXQt, variabel aksesibilitas Qt, menu *Eduka-Orca*, skrip nyala/mati |
+
+Semua nilai di atas hanya **bawaan**: pengguna tetap bisa mengubahnya di
+*Pengaturan Orca* (Orca+Spasi), dan tombol Orca+Shift+D tetap menyalakan/mematikan
+teks ucapan.
+
+## Cara memakai di Eduka-Desktop
+
+* **Menu → Aksesibilitas → Eduka-Orca**: menyalakan atau mematikan pembaca layar.
+  Muncul notifikasi di layar "Eduka-Orca aktif / nonaktif".
+* Dari terminal: `eduka-orca-toggle`, atau `eduka-orca --replace`.
+* Pengaturan: klik kanan menu *Eduka-Orca → Pengaturan*, atau `eduka-orca --replace --setup`.
+* Pilihan nyala/mati diingat: jika aktif, Eduka-Orca otomatis berjalan saat login
+  (`/etc/xdg/autostart/eduka-orca-autostart.desktop`, khusus LXQt).
+* Pintasan keyboard **Super+Alt+S**: gabungkan
+  `/usr/share/eduka-orca/globalkeyshortcuts-eduka-orca.conf` ke
+  `/etc/xdg/lxqt/globalkeyshortcuts.conf` bawaan Eduka-Desktop.
+
+### Menyalakan secara bawaan untuk semua pengguna (untuk pembuat ISO)
+
+Buat berkas `/usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/95_edukasaun-a11y.gschema.override`:
+
+```
+[org.gnome.desktop.a11y.applications]
+screen-reader-enabled=true
+```
+
+lalu jalankan `glib-compile-schemas /usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas`.
+
+### Mengubah kecepatan bawaan untuk seluruh sistem
+
+Buat berkas override, misalnya `96_edukasaun-orca.gschema.override`:
+
+```
+[org.gnome.Orca.Voice]
+rate=25
+pitch=4.5
+
+[org.gnome.Orca.Speech]
+monitor-font-size=28
+```
+
+## Berkas yang dipasang paket ini
+
+* `/usr/bin/orca` — Orca 50.3 dengan patch Eduka
+* `/usr/bin/eduka-orca`, `eduka-orca-toggle`, `eduka-orca-autostart`
+* `/usr/share/applications/eduka-orca.desktop` — entri menu
+* `/etc/xdg/autostart/eduka-orca-autostart.desktop` — autostart LXQt
+* `/etc/profile.d/eduka-orca-a11y.sh`, `/usr/lib/environment.d/90-eduka-orca-a11y.conf`
+  — `QT_ACCESSIBILITY=1` agar aplikasi Qt/LXQt terbaca oleh Orca
+* `/usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/90_eduka-orca.gschema.override`
+
+## Catatan penting tentang gangguan pendengaran
+
+Orca adalah pembaca layar berbasis **suara**. Untuk pengguna yang **tuli total**,
+suara tidak membantu; yang membantu adalah **teks ucapan di layar** yang sekarang
+aktif secara bawaan, ditambah pembesar layar dan tema kontras tinggi. Untuk
+pengguna yang **sulit mendengar**, bicara pelan, nada lebih rendah, dan volume
+maksimum membuat ucapan lebih mudah diikuti. Uji coba bersama pengguna
+tunarungu di sekolah sangat disarankan untuk menyetel angka kecepatan yang paling cocok.
+
+## Kode sumber
+
+Berbasis tag `50.3` dari https://github.com/GNOME/orca (LGPL-2.1-or-later).
+Semua perubahan Eduka ditandai dengan komentar `Eduka-Orca`, nilai bawaan ada di
+`src/orca/eduka_defaults.py`, dan diuji di `tests/unit_tests/test_eduka_defaults.py`.
+
+---
+
+## English summary
+
+Eduka-Orca = Orca 50.3 + these changes: speech rate 30 (upstream 50), pitch 4.5
+(upstream 5.0), speech monitor captions on by default (24 pt yellow on black,
+docked at the bottom, never steals focus, newest line bold, persisted in
+GSettings key `org.gnome.Orca.Speech monitor-enabled`), Tetum locale uses a
+European Portuguese voice, plus LXQt autostart, Qt accessibility environment,
+an "Eduka-Orca" menu entry and an on/off toggle script. Built for Debian 13
+(trixie), which Edukasaun OS follows.
diff --git a/eduka/bin/eduka-orca b/eduka/bin/eduka-orca
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..ef68b62
--- /dev/null
+++ b/eduka/bin/eduka-orca
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Eduka-Orca launcher for Eduka-Desktop (LXQt) on Edukasaun OS.
+#
+# Starts Orca with the Eduka defaults (slow speech, on-screen captions). All
+# arguments are passed through to orca, e.g. "eduka-orca --replace --setup".
+
+# Qt applications (the whole LXQt desktop) expose their accessibility tree to
+# AT-SPI only when this is set. It is also exported session-wide by
+# /etc/profile.d/eduka-orca-a11y.sh; setting it here covers apps Orca spawns.
+export QT_ACCESSIBILITY=1
+
+# Tell GTK and Qt applications started from now on that assistive technology is on.
+if command -v gsettings >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    gsettings set org.gnome.desktop.interface toolkit-accessibility true 2>/dev/null || true
+fi
+
+exec /usr/bin/orca "$@"
diff --git a/eduka/bin/eduka-orca-autostart b/eduka/bin/eduka-orca-autostart
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..ae76075
--- /dev/null
+++ b/eduka/bin/eduka-orca-autostart
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Session autostart helper for Eduka-Desktop (LXQt).
+#
+# lxqt-session does not evaluate the GNOME-only "AutostartCondition" key, so
+# this helper checks the screen-reader setting itself and only starts
+# Eduka-Orca when the user (or the Edukasaun OS installer) turned it on.
+
+enabled=$(gsettings get org.gnome.desktop.a11y.applications screen-reader-enabled 2>/dev/null)
+[ "$enabled" = "true" ] || exit 0
+
+# Give the panel and the AT-SPI bus a moment to come up, so the first thing
+# Orca reads is the desktop and not an empty session.
+sleep "${EDUKA_ORCA_START_DELAY:-2}"
+
+exec /usr/bin/eduka-orca --replace
diff --git a/eduka/bin/eduka-orca-toggle b/eduka/bin/eduka-orca-toggle
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..8dbfe62
--- /dev/null
+++ b/eduka/bin/eduka-orca-toggle
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Turn Eduka-Orca on or off for the current user (Eduka-Desktop / LXQt).
+#
+# Used by the "Eduka-Orca" menu entry and the Super+Alt+S keyboard shortcut.
+# The choice is remembered in GSettings, so Eduka-Orca starts again (or not)
+# at the next login.
+
+SCHEMA=org.gnome.desktop.a11y.applications
+KEY=screen-reader-enabled
+UID_NOW=$(id -u)
+
+say() {
+    # Visual feedback for users who are hard of hearing.
+    if command -v notify-send >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+        notify-send --app-name=Eduka-Orca --icon=orca "Eduka-Orca" "$1" 2>/dev/null || true
+    fi
+}
+
+msg_on() {
+    case "${LANGUAGE:-${LC_ALL:-${LC_MESSAGES:-$LANG}}}" in
+        tet*) echo "Eduka-Orca ativu" ;;
+        pt*) echo "Eduka-Orca ativado" ;;
+        id*) echo "Eduka-Orca aktif" ;;
+        *) echo "Eduka-Orca is on" ;;
+    esac
+}
+
+msg_off() {
+    case "${LANGUAGE:-${LC_ALL:-${LC_MESSAGES:-$LANG}}}" in
+        tet*) echo "Eduka-Orca la ativu" ;;
+        pt*) echo "Eduka-Orca desativado" ;;
+        id*) echo "Eduka-Orca nonaktif" ;;
+        *) echo "Eduka-Orca is off" ;;
+    esac
+}
+
+set_key() {
+    if command -v gsettings >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+        gsettings set "$SCHEMA" "$KEY" "$1" 2>/dev/null || true
+    fi
+}
+
+if pgrep -u "$UID_NOW" -x orca >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    set_key false
+    pkill -TERM -u "$UID_NOW" -x orca
+    say "$(msg_off)"
+else
+    set_key true
+    if command -v setsid >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+        setsid /usr/bin/eduka-orca --replace >/dev/null 2>&1 &
+    else
+        nohup /usr/bin/eduka-orca --replace >/dev/null 2>&1 &
+    fi
+    say "$(msg_on)"
+fi
